{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.chaining",
    "description": "Template library: the arithmetic half of a CHAINED pollutant-process. MOVES computes some pollutants not from a rate table but from another pollutant already computed -- PM2.5 brake wear from PM10 by `PM10EmissionRatio`, NO and NO2 from total NOx by `NONO2Ratio`, crankcase from running by `CrankcaseEmissionRatio`, and the hydrocarbon species from THC by `methaneTHCRatio` and `HCSpeciation`. `runspecchainedto` is the edge list and `pollutantprocessassoc.chainedto1`/`chainedto2` the full graph it is pruned from.\n\nThe chain is a FIXED POINT and not a single hop: a chained pollutant-process can itself be a parent. Measured over every `runspecchainedto` in `../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots`, the longest onroad chain is THREE rungs -- THC (101) to NMHC (7901) to NMOG (8001) to TOG (8601) in `chain-tog-speciation`, and THC to NMHC to VOC (8701) to benzene (2001) in `process-airtoxics` -- and the widest fan-in is TWO parents (TOG is the SUM of methane and NMOG). `process-pm-exhaust` and every nonroad snapshot have chainedto graphs with CYCLES (118 from 115 and 115 from 118), because the table records which pollutants a calculator MAY derive an output from and not which it does; a fixed-point unroll is well defined on those graphs only because it stops after a fixed number of rungs, and docs/esm-conventions.md 71 says why that is the right reading rather than a limitation.\n\nA `faq`'s ranges and join clause are equation-level and no expression template can carry them, so the three passes themselves are spelled out at the call site. What IS shared is the per-pass PREDICATE, which is this file.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "onroad", "chained-pollutants", "template-library"]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "chained_emits": {
      "params": ["survives", "has_chain_ratio", "parent_emits", "bin_is_selected"],
      "body": {
        "op": "max",
        "args": [
          "survives",
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": ["has_chain_ratio",
              { "op": "ifelse", "args": [{ "op": ">", "args": ["parent_emits", 0.0] }, 1.0, 0.0] }] },
            "bin_is_selected"] }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
